        "publishTime": 1331827200000,
        "year": "2012",
        "trackCount": 10,
        "company": "Pinkaide",
        "description": "One year after his debut album Beyond The Memory, July returns with In Love, an album filled with the pure, instrumental sound that defines his music. While his first album included collaborations with powerful vocalists, In Love is a collection of ten instrumental tracks that showcase July’s unique style.\n\nThe album opens with the lyrical melody of “Love Theme,” where piano and strings blend seamlessly to set the tone. The title track, “In Love,” paints a melancholic picture of love, embodying July's signature emotional depth. Pieces like “Hyacinth” and “Walking To Heaven” feature nylon guitar with a somber tone, while “Remember Me” incorporates the erhu, creating a distinctly Eastern sound. The track “December” stands out with its powerful sound, and “Somewhere,” originally released as a single between his first and second albums, is newly arranged for this collection.\n\nWith In Love, July returns to his roots, delivering an album that is sure to be a cherished gift for his listeners. Lean back, close your eyes, and let July’s music carry you into the gentle warmth of spring.",
